div.p:
“Whereas the under signed deputy for the King Kamehameha III did, on the 10th day
                    of may, instant, enter his protest against certain acts of the British
                    commission for the Government of the Sandwich Islands;

“And whereas it now appearing evident to the undersigned that the terms of the
                    compact or treaty entered into on the 25th February, 1843, will not in future be
                    respected by the British commission;
